{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#1", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "21%", "answer": "Based on the chart on page 14 (doc_id 0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf, p014), the \"Time spent on weekends\" infographic shows that in 2010, **21%** of weekend time was spent with family and friends. (Note: the same chart shows the 2005 figure as 35%.)\n\nCitation:\n- doc_id: 0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf, page: 14, bbox: (0.55, 0.35, 0.70, 0.50)", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 14, "bbox": {"x0": 0.55, "y0": 0.35, "x1": 0.7, "y1": 0.5}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p017", "watch_d/p021", "watch_d/p022"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p006", "2023.acl-long.386/p006", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p010", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p004", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p017", "watch_d/p021", "2023.acl-long.386/p017", "watch_d/p022", "2023.acl-long.386/p004", "watch_d/p019", "watch_d/p001", "watch_d/p002", "watch_d/p003", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p016", "2023.acl-long.386/p022", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p006", "2023.acl-long.386/p019", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p014"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 0.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 0.0, "rounds": 5, "calls": 14, "tokens": 142380, "stop_reason": "recover_exhausted", "latency_s": 38.105}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#2", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "0-375 miles", "answer": "In the \"Tracking the West Nile Virus\" chart, the red color represents an approximate distance of **0 - 375 miles** from the Mississippi River.\n\nThis is shown in the legend titled \"Approximate Distance from the Mississippi River (miles)\", where the red swatch is paired with the label \"0 - 375\" (the other bins being 375 - 750 in orange, 750 - 1125 in yellow, and 1125 - 1500 in pale yellow). The main map itself is titled \"Tracking the West Nile Virus\", with the note that \"Height is Based on Number of Confirmed Human Cases\" (shortest prism = 0, tallest prism = 661).", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 9, "bbox": {"x0": 0.585, "y0": 0.58, "x1": 0.735, "y1": 0.79}}, {"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 9, "bbox": {"x0": 0.262, "y0": 0.565, "x1": 0.412, "y1": 0.725}}, {"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 9, "bbox": {"x0": 0.385, "y0": 0.2, "x1": 0.675, "y1": 0.32}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p008", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p008", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p000", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p010", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p004", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "2023.acl-long.386/p011"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 2, "calls": 7, "tokens": 43984, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 15.449}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#3", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "Elements of objects tend to be perceptually grouped together if they form a pattern that is regular, simple, and orderly.", "answer": "According to the document, the law of good Gestalt is defined as follows: \"Elements of objects tend to be perceptually grouped together if they form a pattern that is regular, simple, and orderly.\" The text further explains that this law implies that as individuals perceive the world, \"they eliminate complexity and unfamiliarity so they can observe a reality in its most simplistic form,\" and that \"eliminating extraneous stimuli helps the mind create meaning.\" It adds that the meaning created by perception \"implies a global regularity, which is often mentally prioritized over spatial relations,\" and that \"the law of good gestalt focuses on the idea of conciseness, which is what all of gestalt theory is based on.\"", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 10, "bbox": {"x0": 0.043, "y0": 0.233, "x1": 0.49, "y1": 0.482}}, {"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 10, "bbox": {"x0": 0.043, "y0": 0.519, "x1": 0.493, "y1": 0.663}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p001", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p002", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p000"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p001", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p002", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p000"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 1, "calls": 4, "tokens": 13202, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 4.795}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#4", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "Eating out", "answer": "The category with the most increase from 2005 to 2010 for time spent on weekends is \"With family and friends.\" In the 2005 chart, \"With family and friends\" was 35% (indicated by the legend \"Family and friends\" in the bottom-left corner), while in the 2010 chart it was 21%. The 2005 chart has a slice labeled \"With family and friends 35%\" and the 2010 chart has a corresponding slice labeled \"With family and friends 21%,\" making it the largest category in 2005 before decreasing in 2010. Since the question asks for the most increase, note that the 2005 value (35%) is larger than the 2010 value (21%), indicating a decrease rather than an increase. If interpreting the category that changed the most between the two years, \"With family and friends\" shows the greatest change (a decrease of 14 percentage points).", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 13, "bbox": {"x0": 0.44, "y0": 0.27, "x1": 0.57, "y1": 0.31}}, {"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 13, "bbox": {"x0": 0.45, "y0": 0.54, "x1": 0.57, "y1": 0.6}}, {"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 13, "bbox": {"x0": 0.62, "y0": 0.41, "x1": 0.73, "y1": 0.5}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p006", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "watch_d/p019", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p003", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005", "watch_d/p021", "2023.acl-long.386/p013", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p004", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "2023.acl-long.386/p004", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p006", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "2023.acl-long.386/p017", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p016", "2023.acl-long.386/p005